A skilled looter develops an instinctive awareness of danger, detecting the
subtle signs of hidden traps before blundering into them. This passive skill
operates automatically whenever the thief encounters a trapped door, container,
or other object.

When a trap is present, the detect trap skill checks against the trap's
concealment. Success reveals the trap's presence, allowing the thief to
decide whether to disarm it or avoid triggering it. Failure leaves the
trap hidden, potentially leading to a painful surprise.

The effectiveness of detection depends on the thief's skill level versus
the difficulty of the trap. More sophisticated traps are harder to detect,
but a master looter can spot even the most cunningly concealed mechanisms.
Note that failed detection on an untrapped item may create a "ghost trap"
that appears real until disarmed.

Detect trap is essential for any thief who wishes to survive encounters
with trapped treasures. Even experienced looters sometimes miss traps, so
caution is always advised.

See Also: DISARM TRAP, SET TRAP
